{"id":44743271212483,"type":"album","name":"The River","artist":"Bruce Springsteen","year":1980,"weight":22,"info":{"cover":"https://dn721905.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-a294c8e9-e67c-4ca4-9de9-2303e9531a67/mbid-a294c8e9-e67c-4ca4-9de9-2303e9531a67-36940570982.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":11,"country":"US","scaruffi":8.5,"aoty":94,"aoty_user":81,"yt":"klVu1sf6HO4","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/6YNIEeDWqC09YIWzhoSVLg","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_nm7hctofCJeCbZchWDnOHfoXAxMG7oP2Y","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/bruce-springsteen/the-river","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/5805-bruce-springsteen-the-river.php"},"desc":"The River is the fifth studio album by Bruce Springsteen. It was released on October 17, 1980, by Columbia Records. Springsteen's only double album, The River was produced by Jon Landau, Springsteen, and bandmate Steven Van Zandt. The album was Springsteen's first to go #1 on the Billboard 200 and spent four weeks at the top of chart. \"The River\" was nominated for Best Rock Vocal Performance at the 1982 Grammy Awards. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":168754358908938,"name":"Bruce Springsteen","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bruce_Springsteen_2025.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":106381401668595,"type":"genre","name":"Heartland Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":254,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":115932688871073,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Heartland Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":4,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":8.5},{"id":52032266791182,"name":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":10,"year":null,"note":null,"total":877,"scaruffi":8.5},{"id":215424088090262,"name":"AOTY Must Hear 1980s","src":"charts","grp":"AOTY","list_year":null,"rank":179,"year":1980,"note":null,"total":196,"scaruffi":8.5},{"id":244769911076515,"name":"RYM Top — Singer-Songwriter","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":184,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":8.5}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Work on this double album began in March 1979 and it was eventually released in the fall of 1980, nearly a year after its initial target date of December 1979. The title track delves into the story of a young couple forced into a shotgun wedding due to an unplanned pregnancy, with the young man struggling to find employment, illustrating how the titular river, once a symbol of freedom, became a trap. \"In the title track to the river springstein wrote about a young couple that has to have a shotgun wedding because of an unplanned pregnancy and the young man had a hard time finding a job the river seemed like freedom but ended up being a bit of a trap.\"","year":1980,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 55 - Heartland Rock is about More than the Heartland","url":"https://www.ftr70.com/"},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 55 - Heartland Rock is about More than the Heartland","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":44743271212483,"artist":"Bruce Springsteen","artist_id":168754358908938,"title":"The River","year":1980,"ess":1,"yt":"8xKT8_V2wcE","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los setenta","scene_id":98497937254844,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-70s","chapters":["Sección 4.3"],"pages":[[1,87,null]]}],"others":[{"id":152534608089946,"type":"album","name":"Born In The USA","year":1984,"weight":47},{"id":117235478886941,"type":"album","name":"Nebraska","year":1982,"weight":40},{"id":222148697847766,"type":"album","name":"Born in the U.S.A.","year":1984,"weight":33},{"id":2403782285570,"type":"album","name":"Born To Run","year":1975,"weight":33},{"id":209431782104489,"type":"al